Look up OpenMP by soname on QNX instead of spawning ldconfig and ld

The bundled omp module called ctypes.util.find_library() for omp, gomp
and iomp5 on every import attempt; on QNX that spawns ldconfig, gcc and
ld, none of which a target has (144 failed spawns, about 50 s of each
"import pythran" on an x86_64 VM). The runtime loader is asked directly.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/omp/__init__.py
+++ b/omp/__init__.py
@@ -119,6 +119,20 @@
 
     def init_not_msvc(self):
         """ Find OpenMP library and try to load if using ctype interface. """
+        if sys.platform.startswith('qnx'):
+            # ctypes.util.find_library() finds nothing on QNX and spawns
+            # ldconfig, gcc and ld (none of which a target has) for each
+            # name; there is no compiler to ask either. The runtime loader
+            # finds the library by its soname, if there is one.
+            for libomp_name in self.get_libomp_names():
+                for soname in ('lib%s.so' % libomp_name, 'lib%s.so.1' % libomp_name):
+                    try:
+                        self.libomp = ctypes.CDLL(soname)
+                    except OSError:
+                        continue
+                    self.version = 45
+                    return
+            raise ImportError("I can't find a shared library for libomp")
         # find_library() does not automatically search LD_LIBRARY_PATH
         # until Python 3.6+, so we explicitly add it.
         # LD_LIBRARY_PATH is used on Linux, while macOS uses DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH
